sentiment analysis has 3 stages, Tokenizer-Model-Post Processing



Tokenizer turns everything into numbers
default of sentiment tracker is distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english
to download information from Model Hub, we use:

from transformers import AutoTokenizer

checkpoint = "distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english"
tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(checkpoint)

now you will get a list of dictionary that is ready to feed to the model, convert IDs into Tensors:

raw_inputs = [
    "I've been waiting for a HuggingFace course my whole life.",
    "I hate this so much!",
]
inputs = tokenizer(raw_inputs, padding=True, truncation=True, return_tensors="pt")   #retunr_tensor to specify the tensors we want back
print(inputs)





Download to Model:

from transformers import AutoModel

checkpoint = "distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english"
model = AutoModel.from_pretrained(checkpoint)


